erb", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈkætəl/", "tags": []}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "[ˈkʰæt(ə)ɫ]", "tags": ["Received Pronunciation"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "[ˈkʰæɾ(ə)ɫ]", "tags": ["US"]}], "forms": [{"word": "cattles", "tags": ["present", "singular", "third-person"]}, {"word": "cattling", "tags": ["participle", "present"]}, {"word": "cattled", "tags": ["participle", "past"]}, {"word": "cattled", "tags": ["past"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "(transitive, Cockney rhyming slang) Ellipsis of cattle truck (“to fuck: to break, destroy”).", "tags": ["Cockney", "abbreviation", "alt of", "ellipsis", "slang", "transitive"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "I would talk to rayburn, and the people who converted it..I have assumed from what you said that it was an old coal burner converted...or is it a revamped oil burner? In which case the revampers may have cattled it..", "reference": "2002 February 8, The Natural Philosopher, “Re: Rayburn problems”, in uk.d-i-y (Usenet):"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}], "source": {"url": "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cattle", "license": {"name": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"}}}}